est-xdist is not installed\n209 |         return\n210 |     else:\n211 |         xdist_worker_count = int(xdist_worker_count)\n212 | \n213 |     openmp_threads = _openmp_effective_n_threads()\n214 |     threads_per_worker = max(openmp_threads // xdist_worker_count, 1)\n215 |     threadpool_limits(threads_per_worker, user_api=\"openmp\")\n```\n\nFound function `sklearn/conftest.py:pytest_configure`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n218 | def pytest_configure(config):\n219 |     # Use matplotlib agg backend during the tests including doctests\n220 |     try:\n221 |         import matplotlib\n222 | \n223 |         matplotlib.use(\"agg\")\n224 |     except ImportError:\n225 |         pass\n```\n\nFound file `sklearn/utils/extmath.py`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\nHint: Search `sklearn/utils/extmath.py` for the full content if needed.\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"matplotlib\", \"matplotlib plt\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `sklearn/utils/__init__.py:check_matplotlib_support`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n1085 | def check_matplotlib_support(caller_name):\n1086 |     \"\"\"Raise ImportError with detailed error message if mpl is not installed.\n1087 | \n1088 |     Plot utilities like :func:`plot_partial_dependence` should lazily import\n1089 |     matplotlib and call this helper before any computation.\n1090 | \n1091 |     Parameters\n1092 |     ----------\n1093 |     caller_name : str\n1094 |         The name of the caller that requires matplotlib.\n1095 |     \"\"\"\n1096 |     try:\n1097 |         import matplotlib  # noqa\n1098 |     except ImportError as e:\n1099 |         raise ImportError(\n1100 |             \"{} requires matplotlib. You can install matplotlib with \"\n1101 |             \"`pip install matplotlib`\".format(caller_name)\n1102 |         ) from e\n```\n\nFound function `doc/conftest.py:skip_if_matplotlib_not_installed`.\nSource: Retrieved entity usi