            ax = fig.add_subplot(gs[i, 0:max_left_cols])\n 80 |                 self._make_table(ax, l, title=label, height=1.0 / max_left_rows)\n 81 |             # right\n 82 |             ax = plt.subplot(gs[:, max_left_cols:])\n 83 |             self._make_table(ax, right, title=\"Result\", height=1.05 / vcells)\n 84 |             fig.subplots_adjust(top=0.9, bottom=0.05, left=0.05, right=0.95)\n 85 |         else:\n 86 |             max_rows = max(self._shape(df)[0] for df in left + [right])\n 87 |             height = 1.0 / np.max(max_rows)\n 88 |             gs = gridspec.GridSpec(1, hcells)\n 89 |             # left\n 90 |             i = 0\n 91 |             for df, label in zip(left, labels):\n 92 |                 sp = self._shape(df)\n 93 |                 ax = fig.add_subplot(gs[0, i : i + sp[1]])\n 94 |                 self._make_table(ax, df, title=label, height=height)\n 95 |                 i += sp[1]\n 96 |             # right\n 97 |             ax = plt.subplot(gs[0, i:])\n 98 |             self._make_table(ax, right, title=\"Result\", height=height)\n 99 |             fig.subplots_adjust(top=0.85, bottom=0.05, left=0.05, right=0.95)\n100 | \n101 |         return fig\n```\n\nFound function `pandas/core/frame.py:DataFrame.T`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n3468 | def T(self) -> DataFrame:\n3469 |         return self.transpose()\n```\n\nFound function `pandas/plotting/_core.py:PlotAccessor.barh`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n1207 | def barh(self, x=None, y=None, **kwargs):\n1208 |         \"\"\"\n1209 |         Make a horizontal bar plot.\n1210 | \n1211 |         A horizontal bar plot is a plot that presents quantitative data with\n1212 |         rectangular bars with lengths proportional to the values that they\n1213 |         represent. A bar plot shows comparisons among discrete categories. One\n1214 |         axis of the plot shows the specific categories being compared, and the