|     Parameters\n1476 |     ----------\n1477 |     prefer_skip_nested_validation : bool\n1478 |         If True, the validation of parameters of inner estimators or functions\n1479 |         called during fit will be skipped.\n1480 | \n1481 |         This is useful to avoid validating many times the parameters passed by the\n1482 |         user from the public facing API. It's also useful to avoid validating\n1483 |         parameters that we pass internally to inner functions that are guaranteed to\n1484 |         be valid by the test suite.\n1485 | \n1486 |         It should be set to True for most estimators, except for those that receive\n1487 |         non-validated objects as parameters, such as meta-estimators that are given\n1488 |         estimator objects.\n1489 | \n1490 |     Returns\n1491 |     -------\n1492 |     decorated_fit : method\n1493 |         The decorated fit method.\n1494 |     \"\"\"\n1495 | \n1496 |     def decorator(fit_method):\n1497 |         @functools.wraps(fit_method)\n1498 |         def wrapper(estimator, *args, **kwargs):\n1499 |             global_skip_validation = get_config()[\"skip_parameter_validation\"]\n1500 | \n1501 |             # we don't want to validate again for each call to partial_fit\n1502 |             partial_fit_and_fitted = (\n1503 |                 fit_method.__name__ == \"partial_fit\" and _is_fitted(estimator)\n1504 |             )\n1505 | \n1506 |             if not global_skip_validation and not partial_fit_and_fitted:\n1507 |                 estimator._validate_params()\n1508 | \n1509 |             with config_context(\n1510 |                 skip_parameter_validation=(\n1511 |                     prefer_skip_nested_validation or global_skip_validation\n1512 |                 )\n1513 |             ):\n1514 |                 return fit_method(estimator, *args, **kwargs)\n1515 | \n1516 |         return wrapper\n1517 | \n1518 |     return decorator\n```\n"}, {"content": "Let me check the execution trace artif