the `classes` parameter is set, `y` will not be\n849 |             iterated.\n850 | \n851 |         Returns\n852 |         -------\n853 |         y_indicator : array or CSR matrix, shape (n_samples, n_classes)\n854 |             A matrix such that `y_indicator[i, j] = 1` iff `classes_[j]` is in\n855 |             `y[i]`, and 0 otherwise.\n856 |         \"\"\"\n857 |         check_is_fitted(self)\n858 | \n859 |         class_to_index = self._build_cache()\n860 |         yt = self._transform(y, class_to_index)\n861 | \n862 |         if not self.sparse_output:\n863 |             yt = yt.toarray()\n864 | \n865 |         return yt\n```\n\nFound function `sklearn/preprocessing/_label.py:MultiLabelBinarizer._build_cache`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n867 | def _build_cache(self):\n868 |         if self._cached_dict is None:\n869 |             self._cached_dict = dict(zip(self.classes_, range(len(self.classes_))))\n870 | \n871 |         return self._cached_dict\n```\n\nFound file `sklearn/utils/_set_output.py`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\nHint: Search `sklearn/utils/_set_output.py` for the full content if needed.\n"}, {"content": "Let's also check the parent class structure:\n\n<function=search_code_snippets>\n<parameter=search_terms>['TransformerMixin', 'BaseEstimator']</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "search_code_snippets", "content": "OBSERVATION:\n##Searching for term \"TransformerMixin\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound class `sklearn/base.py:TransformerMixin`.\nSource: Match found for entity name `TransformerMixin`.\n```\n864 | class TransformerMixin(_SetOutputMixin):\n865 |     \"\"\"Mixin class for all transformers in scikit-learn.\n866 | \n867 |     If :term:`get_feature_names_out` is defined, then `BaseEstimator` will\n868 |     automatically wrap `transform` and `fit_transform` to follow the `set_output`\n869 |     API. See the :ref:`developer_api_set_output` for details.\n870 | \n871 |     :class:`base.OneToOneFeatureMixin` and\n872 |     :class:`base.ClassNamePrefixFeaturesOutMixin` are helpful mixins for\n873 |     defining :term:`get_feature_names_out`.\n874 |     \"\"\"\n875 | \n876 |     def fit_transform(self, X, y=None, **fit_params):\n877 |         \"\"\"\n878 |         Fit to data, then transform it.\n879 | \n880 |         Fits transformer to `X` and `y` with optional parameters `fit_params`\n881 |         and returns a transformed version of `X`.\n882 | \n883 |         Parameters\n884 |         ----------\n885 |         X : array-like of shape (n_samples, n_features)\n886 |             Input samples.\n887 | \n888 |         y :  array-like of shape (n_samples,) or (n_samples, n_outputs), \\\n889 |                 default=None\n890 |             Target values (None for unsupervised transformations).\n891 | \n892 |         **fit_params : dict\n893 |             Additional fit parameters.\n894 | \n895 |         Returns\n896 |         -------\n897 |         X_new : ndarray array of shape (n_samples, n_features_new)\n898 |             Transformed array.\n899 |         \"\"\"\n900 |         # non-optimized default implementation; override when a better\n901 |         # method is possible for a given clustering algorithm\n902 |         if y is None:\n903 |             # fit method of arity 1 (unsupervised transformation)\n904 |             return self.fit(X, **fit_params).transform(X)\n905 |         else:\n906 |             # fit method of arity 2 (supervised transformation)\n907 |             return self.fit(X, y, **fit_params).transform(X)\n```\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"BaseEstimator\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound class `sklearn/base.py:BaseEstimator`.\nSource: Match found for entity name `BaseEstimator`.\nJust show the structure of this class due to response length limitations:\n```\nclass BaseEstimator:\n\n    @classmethod\n    def _get_param_names(cls):\n...\n    def get_params(self, deep=True):\n...\n    def set_params(self, **params):\n...\n    def __sklearn_clone__(self):\n...\n    def __repr__(self, N_CHAR_MAX=700):\n...\n    def __getstate__(self):\n...\n    def __setstate__(self, state):\n...\n    def _more_tags(self):\n...\n    def _get_tags(self):\n...\n    def _check_n_features(self, X, reset):\n...\n    def _check_feature_names(self, X, *, reset):\n...\n    def _validate_data(\n        self,\n        X=\"no_validation\",\n        y=\"no_validation\",\n        reset=True,\n        validate_separately=False,\n        cast_to_ndarray=True,\n        **check_params,\n    ):\n...\n    def _validate_params(self):\n...\n    @property\n    def _repr_html_(self):\n...\n    def _repr_html_inner(self):\n...\n    def _repr_mimebundle_(self, **kwargs):\n\n```\nHint: Search `sklearn/base.py:BaseEstimator` to get the full content if needed.\n"}, {"content": "After thorough analysis of the codebase and the issue, I can confirm that the previously identified locations are indeed comprehensive enough to implement sparse matrix output in SplineTransformer. Let me summarize and refine the locations block:\n\n```\nsklearn/preprocessing/_polynomial.py\nline: 693-702\nclass: SplineTransformer\nfunction: __init__\n\nsklearn/preprocessing/_polynomial.py\nline: 919-921\nclass: SplineTransformer\nfunction: fit\n\nsklearn/preprocessing/_polynomial.py\nline: 943-950\nclass: SplineTransformer\nfunction: transform\n\nsklearn/utils/extmath.py\nline: 160-202\nfunction: safe_sparse_dot\n\nsklearn/preprocessing/_label.py\nline: 434-596\nfunction: label_binarize\n```\n\nThis collection of locations covers all essential components needed to implement sparse matrix output:\n1. The primary initialization of the transformer (SplineTransformer.__init__)\n2. The data fitting process (SplineTransformer.fit)\n3. The transformation logic (SplineTransformer.transform)\n4. The sparse matrix utility functions (utils.extmath.safe_sparse_dot)\n5. The