ags_provider.klass\",\n    \"sklearn/utils/_tags.py:_find_tags_provider.OrderedDict -> sklearn/utils/_tags.py:_find_tags_provider.tags_mro -> sklearn/utils/_tags.py:_find_tags_provider.tags_mro[]\",\n    \"sklearn/utils/_tags.py:_find_tags_provider.OrderedDict -> sklearn/utils/_tags.py:_find_tags_provider.tags_mro -> sklearn/utils/_tags.py:_find_tags_provider.all_providers\"\n  ],\n  \"has_more\": true,\n  \"next_start\": 12\n}"}, {"content": "Let me analyze the implementation details.\n\n<function=get_entity_contents>\n<parameter=entity_names>['sklearn/utils/_tags.py:get_tags', 'sklearn/utils/estimator_checks.py:check_estimator_tags_renamed', 'sklearn/base.py:BaseEstimator.__sklearn_tags__']</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "get_entity_contents", "content": "OBSERVATION:\n##Searching for entity `sklearn/utils/_tags.py:get_tags`...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `sklearn/utils/_tags.py:get_tags`.\nSource: Exact match found for entity name `sklearn/utils/_tags.py:get_tags`.\n```\n293 | def get_tags(estimator) -> Tags:\n294 |     \"\"\"Get estimator tags.\n295 | \n296 |     :class:`~sklearn.BaseEstimator` provides the estimator tags machinery.\n297 |     However, if an estimator does not inherit from this base class, we should\n298 |     fall-back to the default tags.\n299 | \n300 |     For scikit-learn built-in estimators, we should still rely on\n301 |     `self.__sklearn_tags__()`. `get_tags(est)` should be used when we\n302 |     are not sure where `est` comes from: typically\n303 |     `get_tags(self.estimator)` where `self` is a meta-estimator, or in\n304 |     the common checks.\n305 | \n306 |     .. versionadded:: 1.6\n307 | \n308 |     Parameters\n309 |     ----------\n310 |     estimator : estimator object\n311 |         The estimator from which to get the tag.\n312 | \n313 |     Returns\n314 |     -------\n315 |     tags : :class:`~.sklearn.utils.Tags`\n316 |         The estimator tags.\n317 |     \"\"\"\n318 | \n319 |     if hasattr(estimator, \"__sklearn_tags__\"):\n320 |         tags = estimator.__sklearn_tags__()\n321 |     else:\n322 |         warnings.warn(\n323 |             f\"Estimator {estimator} has no __sklearn_tags__ attribute, which is \"\n324 |             \"defined in `sklearn.base.BaseEstimator`. This will raise an error in \"\n325 |             \"scikit-learn 1.8. Please define the __sklearn_tags__ method, or inherit \"\n326 |             \"from `sklearn.base.BaseEstimator` and other appropriate mixins such as \"\n327 |             \"`sklearn.base.TransformerMixin`, `sklearn.base.ClassifierMixin`, \"\n328 |             \"`sklearn.base.RegressorMixin`, and `sklearn.base.ClusterMixin`, and \"\n329 |             \"`sklearn.base.OutlierMixin`.\",\n330 |             category=FutureWarning,\n331 |         )\n332 |         tags = default_tags(estimator)\n333 | \n334 |     return tags\n```\n\n\n##Searching for entity `sklearn/utils/estimator_checks.py:check_estimator_tags_renamed`...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `sklearn/utils/estimator_checks.py:check_estimator_tags_renamed`.\nSource: Exact match found for entity name `sklearn/utils/estimator_checks.py:check_estimator_tags_renamed`.\n```\n4447 | def check_estimator_tags_renamed(name, estimator_orig):\n4448 |     help = \"\"\"{tags_func}() was removed in 1.6. Please use __sklearn_tags__ instead.\n4449 | You can implement both __sklearn_tags__() and {tags_func}() to support multiple\n4450 | scikit-learn versions.\n4451 | \"\"\"\n4452 | \n4453 |     for klass in type(estimator_orig).mro():\n4454 |         if (\n4455 |             # Here we check vars(...) because we want to check if the method is\n4456 |             # explicitly defined in the class instead of inherited from a parent class.\n4457 |             (\"_more_tags\" in vars(klass) or \"_get_tags\" in vars(klass))\n4458 |             and \"__sklearn_tags__\" not in vars(klass)\n4459 |         ):\n4460 |             raise TypeError(\n4461 |                 f\"Estimator {name} has defined either `_more_tags` or `_get_tags`,\"\n4462 |                 \" but not `__sklearn_tags__`. If you're customizing tags, and need to\"\n4463 |                 \" support multiple scikit-learn versions, you can implement both\"\n4464 |                 \" `__sklearn_tags__` and `_more_tags` or `_get_tags`. This change was\"\n4465 |                 \" introduced in scikit-learn=1.6\"\n4466 |             )\n```\n\n\n##Searching for entity `sklearn/base.py:BaseEstimator.__sklearn_tags__`...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `sklearn/base.py:BaseEstimator.__sklearn_tags__`.\nSource: Exact match found for entity name `sklearn/base.py:BaseEstimator.__sklearn_tags__`.\n```\n392 | def __sklearn_tags__(self):\n393 |         return Tags(\n394 |             estimator_type=None,\n395 |             target_tags=TargetTags(required=False),\n396 |             transformer_tags=None,\n397 |             regressor_tags=None,\n398 |             classifier_tags=None,\n399 |         )\n```\n"}, {"content": "Based on my analysis, here are the key locations that need modification to implement the old/new tags conversion feature:\n\n```\nsklearn/utils/_tags.py\nline: 293-334\nfunction: get_tags\n\nsklearn/utils/estimator_checks.py\nline: 4447-4466\nfunction: check_estimator_tags_renamed\n\nsklearn/base.py\nline: 392-399\nfunction: BaseEstimator.__sklearn_tags__\n\nsklearn/utils/_tags.py\nline: 319-332\nfunction: get_tags\n\nsklearn/utils/validation.py\nline: 2899-2916\nfunction: validate_data\n```\n\nThe issue requires implementing:\n1. A way to convert old-style (`_get_tags`, `_more_tags`) to new-style (`__sklearn_tags__`)\n2. Handling cases where an estimator implements only the old or new tags\n3. Warning when BaseEstimator is used directly without implementing the new tags\n4. Deprecating _safe_tags while maintaining compatibility\n\nThe main changes needed are in these files, particularly focusing on:\n1. The `get_tags` function which is the core implementation that determines how tags are retrieved\n2. The `check_estimator_tags_renamed` function which enforces the new tagging system\n3. The base `BaseEstimator` class which defines the new tagging interface\n4. The validation helpers that use the tags system\n5. Any dependent modules that might need to be updated to handle the new tagging system\n\nThe implementation should:\n- Detect when an estimator uses old-style tags and provide a fallback to new-style when possible\n- Raise warnings when deprecated features are used\n- Properly handle the case where a BaseEstimator is used directly rather than a child class implementing the new tags\n- Maintain backward compatibility while providing a migration path for old-style tags", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "user", "content": "Verify if the found locations contain all the necessary information to address the issue, and check for any relevant references in other parts of the codebase that may not have appeared in the search results. If not, continue searching for additional locations related to the issue.\nVerify that you have carefully analyzed the impact of the found locations on the repository, especially their dependencies. If you think you have solved the task, rewrite your final answer into the required location-only format, output ONLY the location block, and then call `finish` to finish.\nIMPORTANT: YOU SHOULD NEVER ASK FOR HUMAN HELP.\nDaLIC raw evidence tools remain available throughout the investigation.\nIf your current evidence is either too broad, too few or incomplete, call `get_trace_artifacts` or `get_trace_data_dependencies` again with more precise filters before finishing.\n"}, {"content": "Let me verify the completeness of the findings and analyze additional dependencies.\n\n<function=search_code_snippets>\n<parameter=search_terms>['_get_tags', '_more_tags', '__sklearn_tags__', 'get_tags', 