me` objects.\n1422 | \n1423 |         The time part of the Timestamps.\n1424 | \n1425 |         See Also\n1426 |         --------\n1427 |         DatetimeIndex.timetz : Returns numpy array of :class:`datetime.time`\n1428 |             objects with timezones. The time part of the Timestamps.\n1429 |         DatetimeIndex.date : Returns numpy array of python :class:`datetime.date`\n1430 |             objects. Namely, the date part of Timestamps without time and timezone\n1431 |             information.\n1432 | \n1433 |         Examples\n1434 |         --------\n1435 |         For Series:\n1436 | \n1437 |         >>> s = pd.Series([\"1/1/2020 10:00:00+00:00\", \"2/1/2020 11:00:00+00:00\"])\n1438 |         >>> s = pd.to_datetime(s)\n1439 |         >>> s\n1440 |         0   2020-01-01 10:00:00+00:00\n1441 |         1   2020-02-01 11:00:00+00:00\n1442 |         dtype: datetime64[s, UTC]\n1443 |         >>> s.dt.time\n1444 |         0    10:00:00\n1445 |         1    11:00:00\n1446 |         dtype: object\n1447 | \n1448 |         For DatetimeIndex:\n1449 | \n1450 |         >>> idx = pd.DatetimeIndex(\n1451 |         ...     [\"1/1/2020 10:00:00+00:00\", \"2/1/2020 11:00:00+00:00\"]\n1452 |         ... )\n1453 |         >>> idx.time\n1454 |         array([datetime.time(10, 0), datetime.time(11, 0)], dtype=object)\n1455 |         \"\"\"\n1456 |         # If the Timestamps have a timezone that is not UTC,\n1457 |         # convert them into their i8 representation while\n1458 |         # keeping their timezone and not using UTC\n1459 |         timestamps = self._local_timestamps()\n1460 | \n1461 |         return ints_to_pydatetime(timestamps, box=\"time\", reso=self._creso)\n```\n\nFound function `pandas/core/indexes/accessors.py:TimedeltaProperties.to_pytimedelta`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n441 | def to_pytimedelta(self) -> np.ndarray:\n442 |         \"\"\"\n443 |         Return an array of native :class:`datetime.timedelta` objects.\