ibutes.\n141 | \n142 |     Prevents additional attributes via xxx.attribute = \"something\" after a\n143 |     call to `self.__freeze()`. Mainly used to prevent the user from using\n144 |     wrong attributes on an accessor (`Series.cat/.str/.dt`).\n145 | \n146 |     If you really want to add a new attribute at a later time, you need to use\n147 |     `object.__setattr__(self, key, value)`.\n148 |     \"\"\"\n149 | \n150 |     def _freeze(self) -> None:\n151 |         \"\"\"\n152 |         Prevents setting additional attributes.\n153 |         \"\"\"\n154 |         object.__setattr__(self, \"__frozen\", True)\n155 | \n156 |     # prevent adding any attribute via s.xxx.new_attribute = ...\n157 |     def __setattr__(self, key: str, value) -> None:\n158 |         # _cache is used by a decorator\n159 |         # We need to check both 1.) cls.__dict__ and 2.) getattr(self, key)\n160 |         # because\n161 |         # 1.) getattr is false for attributes that raise errors\n162 |         # 2.) cls.__dict__ doesn't traverse into base classes\n163 |         if getattr(self, \"__frozen\", False) and not (\n164 |             key == \"_cache\"\n165 |             or key in type(self).__dict__\n166 |             or getattr(self, key, None) is not None\n167 |         ):\n168 |             raise AttributeError(f\"You cannot add any new attribute '{key}'\")\n169 |         object.__setattr__(self, key, value)\n```\n\nFound file `pandas/core/tools/times.py`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\nHint: Search `pandas/core/tools/times.py` for the full content if needed.\n"}, {"content": "Let me get the full content of the key files:\n\n<function=get_entity_contents>\n<parameter=entity_names>['pandas/core/arrays/datetimes.py:DatetimeArray', 'pandas/core/series.py:Series.round']</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "get_entity_contents", "content": "OBSERVATION:\n##Searching